{
  "subtype": "focus_inference",
  "implied_focus": "Perceived airline experience quality — a qualitative, review-derived assessment of the flight across a few evaluative dimensions (crew/service, seat comfort, value, service reliability).",
  "per_column": [
    {
      "name": "crew_professionalism_assessment",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Qualitative categorization of staff conduct (exceptional/indifferent/rude/standard) — a clear service facet of the experience-quality framing, going beyond the numeric 'Staff Service' rating by naming behavioural modes."
    },
    {
      "name": "seat_physical_comfort",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Categorizes the physical seating experience (comfortable/adequate/cramped/broken) — a distinct comfort facet, adding a 'broken_defective' state absent from the numeric 'Seat Comfort' rating."
    },
    {
      "name": "value_for_money_perception",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Qualitative value judgement (poor/good/excellent/not_worth_premium) — a value facet, largely re-encoding the existing 'Value For Money' rating but with a premium-expectation nuance."
    },
    {
      "name": "service_consistency_reliability",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Assesses reliability/consistency of service (reliable/unpredictable/declining) — a service facet, but conceptually overlaps heavily with crew_professionalism, so it does not cleanly add an independent dimension."
    }
  ],
  "focus_coherence": 0.55,
  "structure_quality": 0.5,
  "focus_actionability": 0.7,
  "rationale": "The four columns are not noise — they are all qualitative, text-inferable evaluative dimensions of the flying experience, so they share a broad theme of 'perceived airline experience quality.' However, the focus-inference mandate is to PROPOSE ONE coherent focus, and here the system instead spread across several top-level aspects (crew, seat, value, reliability) rather than committing to a single focus and decomposing IT. This reads more like a menu of candidate aspects — the very indecision the analyst expressed — than a sharply centred focus, so coherence is only moderate. Structurally the facets are useful in granularity (they add nuanced categories like 'broken_defective', 'declining', 'not_worth_premium'), but three of them (crew, seat, value) essentially re-encode existing numeric columns (Staff Service, Seat Comfort, Value For Money), and crew_professionalism vs service_consistency are near-duplicative on the service dimension, weakening the differentiation and novelty of the structure. The implied focus (experience/service quality) is genuinely actionable — an analyst could investigate its drivers and link to Overall Rating / Recommended — hence the higher actionability score, though it is somewhat blunted by the redundancy with pre-existing ratings."
}
```

